> o I  killed my first  Dragon, zapped  a polymorph on  the dead  meat --
>   and got a can of food... :-( Not exactly what I've expected to get.

    Sometimes they will leavve a "set of dragon scales" when you kill
    them.  Wear 'em and Enchant 'em.

>   And  more important: How can I get  my badly needed grey dragon scale
>   mail??

    Either by the above method (kill one) or wish forr.  But be sure to
    spell it "gray" and not "grey."

> o Another  question: How can I get holy  water? throwing it on a lawful
>   altar doesn't work anymore... :-(

    Put water on your own altar and #pray.  If you're in good standing
    it will be turned into holy water.

> o Also  interesting:  I  haven't  been  able  to  polypile  a  wand  of
>   polymorph... Is this not possible anymore?

    Yeah, but sometimes items are destroyed by polymorphing them.  

> o Then I tried to get Excalibur. I have a blessed rustproof long sword,
>   I have luck (luckstone) and I have plenty of fountains. BUT NO WAY TO
>   GET EXCALIBUR... (I tried at least 50 times... quite annoying.) 

    In 3.1 you must be lawful to #dip a longsword for Excalibur.  I
    think the old rule also applies that you need to be at least x.p.
    level 5 or greater.

